.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH rev-stealth-auth-delete 1  "rev-stealth-auth-delete " 
.SH NAME
rev\-stealth\-auth\-delete \- Delete a profile with shred\-on\-delete
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrev\-stealth auth delete\fR [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-explain\fR] [\fB\-\-idempotency\-key\fR] <\fB\-\-profile\fR> [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Delete a profile with best\-effort shred\-on\-delete (overwrite then unlink). Refuses without \-\-force when stdin is a TTY; \-\-force is required for non\-interactive use.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
v1.3 Lane G.5: side\-effect\-free plan emission. No file writes, no network calls, no keyring operations. Returns exit 0 after emitting the structured plan envelope
.TP
\fB\-\-explain\fR
v1.3 Lane G.5: include the action plan in the result envelope\*(Aqs `result.plan` field. Can be combined with `\-\-dry\-run`. When passed without `\-\-dry\-run`, the plan is emitted alongside the real action
.TP
\fB\-\-idempotency\-key\fR \fI<IDEMPOTENCY_KEY>\fR
v1.3 Lane G.5 / G.6: opaque caller\-supplied key for at\-most\-once commit semantics. Accepted in G.5; surfaced in the envelope; the underlying commit replay semantics land in G.6
.TP
\fB\-\-profile\fR \fI<PROFILE>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Skip the interactive confirmation prompt
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:
  $ rev\-stealth auth delete \-\-profile work
  $ rev\-stealth auth delete \-\-profile work \-\-force

EXIT CODES:
  0  Ok               Profile removed.
  1  UserError        Bad args / user declined / unknown profile.
  3  PermanentError   AuthStore unavailable / shred IO failure.

ENV:
  REV_SCRAPING_AUTH_DIR        Override the AuthStore directory.
